<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-exact-identity-effects> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive the exact parent, commit and tree from local Git object bytes. For complete-carrier-diff coverage, derive the complete carrier denominator and require every effect to appear exactly once as included or excluded. For exact-selected-path-subdiff coverage, bind only the exact declared selected paths and their tree-entry effects, require the separately declared complete carrier path count, and make no classification or adoption claim about every unselected effect. In both modes bind change kind, conditional preimage and postimage SHA-256 digests and modes; refuse missing selected effects, duplicate paths, ambiguous renames or a count/classification mismatch." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-admission-receipt-binding> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-admission-receipt-binding> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "When the selected carrier adoption declares an existing tracked admission receipt, load it through its declared schema, recompute its exact content and receipt digests and bind its path, transition and algorithm; when not declared, bind not-applicable and forbid fabricated receipt fields." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-current-postimage> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-current-postimage> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "For every selected path, independently derive the carrier postimage and one point-in-time repository postimage state at an exact clean relevant HEAD commit/tree basis, using conditional present/absent digest and mode fields. Per-path observedCurrentnessDisposition is exact-present, exact-absent, missing, divergent or unexpected-present according to the exact state/digest/mode comparison. Receipt aggregate observedCurrentnessDisposition is current exactly when every included path is exact-present or exact-absent; otherwise it is reconstructable because the authenticated carrier tree supplies the exact included postimages. Excluded selected effects remain classified and digest-bound but never enter the included-adoption aggregate. Later live scoped currentness uses the same rule against a newly derived clean HEAD basis only in the command result and never rewrites the receipt." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-authority-validation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-authority-validation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Bind the integration authority named-graph identity and its full digest as a point-in-time observation, but derive adoption currentness only from the exact selected manifest identity, selected profile identity/version and a scoped dependency digest over this algorithm, command, permission, receipt and path-effect schemas, selected carrier-adoption, lineage, path-effect-set, currentness authority and every graph-declared validation resource plus exact file/tool dependencies. Unrelated resources in the integration graph and unrelated Git movement cannot stale or regenerate the receipt; caller claims and Git metadata alone are never authority." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-receipt-promotion> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-receipt-promotion> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "For an absent target, prepare one closed-schema content-bound HistoricalCarrierObservation in bounded ignored transient state, rederive and read back every field, then atomically create the same exact bytes at the graph-declared tracked path only under the finite observation-publication permission and remove the transient state. For an existing target, authenticate the stored historical bytes and create nothing. Transient preparation is non-authoritative; a refusal writes no tracked carrier observation. The tracked file is the only durable output and is categorically ineligible for generic completion-evidence loading despite its durable evidence/ directory placement." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-durable-reachability> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-durable-reachability> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Before verification or adoption, authenticate the exact local Git parent, commit and tree objects, require the declared parent relationship and require the carrier commit to be an ancestor of the current clean relevant HEAD basis. Bind that reachability basis commit/tree and outcome in the receipt. Reachability must follow ordinary raw parent edges from current HEAD with replacement, graft, shallow, alternate and partial-clone/filter effects refused; dangling or reflog-only presence is insufficient. Never fetch or contact a remote. Later descendant movement does not invalidate the historical reachability observation." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-scrubbed-git-objects> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-scrubbed-git-objects> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Resolve the repository's common Git directory and object format, require SHA-1 for these three declared 40-hex carriers, set GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1, ignore system/global Git configuration, require refs/replace empty, and reject any info/grafts file, shallow boundary, object alternates environment or file, extensions.partialClone, promisor remote, partial-clone filter or promisor pack used by the object walk. Read raw commit, tree and blob objects without text conversion or filters; independently recompute each Git object ID from type, byte length and raw bytes. The carrier commit must contain exactly one tree header equal to carrierTree and exactly one parent header equal to carrierParentCommit. Parse raw tree entries to derive selected modes and blob IDs, derive each content SHA-256 from raw blob bytes, and require every validation dependency file in the detached worktree to be byte-identical to its authenticated raw carrier blob so attributes, encodings or checkout filters cannot change the executed basis. No fetch, lazy object retrieval, package install, hook, filter, smudge/clean command, remote helper or network operation is permitted." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-normalized-validation-results> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-normalized-validation-results> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Execute only the selected adoption's graph-declared historical carrier validations in an authenticated detached local worktree at the exact carrier commit/tree. Each command must be the supported closed Node test form: exact node, --test, optional graph-declared --test-isolation=none and --test-name-pattern=<literal>, followed only by explicit repository-relative .test.ts files; no shell, glob, eval, package manager or arbitrary flag is allowed. Run it through the graph-declared scrubbed no-network confinement. The carrier tree and packages remain read-only; the only writable bytes are the per-validation scratch tree exposed at /usf-scratch and its initially empty workspace-state child mounted at /workspace/.usf for exact ignored repository-local test state. The dependency member set contains one canonical full carrier-tree member, each exact graph-declared carrier test path and declared receipt/schema input selected for that validation, the complete package dependency closure from the carrier's exact pnpm lock including the root importer's test dev dependencies, exact Git/Node/bwrap host tools, validation/environment/mode/confinement resources and timeout policy. The current file-based authority manifest is bound separately by authorityManifestPath plus its exact raw digest, and the finite selected semantic closure is bound by scopedAuthorityDependencyDigest; neither is falsely required to pre-exist inside an older carrier tree, and unrelated manifest-source bytes cannot become a reproof dependency. The authenticated full carrier tree binds all repository-relative ESM implementation imports, so this bounded command does not add a second TypeScript/import parser. Missing, mutable, filtered, network-fetched or outside-carrier dependencies refuse. A successful tracked receipt contains only the closed deterministic passing result fields and empty failure set defined by the validation-result schema. Current implementation full-suite and containment checks remain carrier-intent qualification gates and never become historical carrier receipt validations. Raw output, timestamps, durations and variable TAP timing remain bounded transient ignored observations and cannot affect tracked receipt bytes." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-target-state-branching> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-target-state-branching> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Authenticate the graph-declared tracked target before choosing exactly one branch. If absent, derive a new receipt from the current authority, raw carrier objects, passing historical validations and a point-in-time clean HEAD observation, then adopt may no-replace-create it. If a regular contained target exists, validate its closed bytes and receipt digest, reconstruct every historical current-postimage field from its recorded currentObservationBasisCommit/tree rather than current files, authenticate that basis and all immutable graph/carrier/validation bindings, and never regenerate or replace it. In both branches derive a separate fresh clean-HEAD live currentness basis and aggregate for the command result only. A symlink, nonregular file, different receipt, invalid historical basis or ambiguous state refuses without any tracked write." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-receipt-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-receipt-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Authenticate every transient ancestor as repository-contained, owner-controlled and non-symlink, require owner-only directory and file modes, refuse hardlinks, nonregular files, hostile replacements and oversized content, and never place secrets in receipt bytes. Preparation receipts, scratch, raw output, per-adoption locks and detached workspaces are bounded transient ignored state and must be removed before successful return; interrupted remnants are authenticated then removed or quarantined before reuse and never become authority. The detached Git worktree may create only its exact matching administrative directory and private index beneath the common Git directory, both removed with the worktree; primary refs and the primary index are immutable. Authenticate the tracked ancestor chain separately, fsync/read back the absent-target receipt and create it with no replacement. That tracked HistoricalCarrierObservation is the only durable output; an authenticated existing target is idempotent matching without any write." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-lock-minimization> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-lock-minimization> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Perform Git inspection, path derivation, detached-worktree validation and transient preparation outside every shared mutation lock. Use at most one owner-private per-adoption transient ignored lock for same-target preparation. For absent-target adopt, hold the existing narrow repository primary-mutation lock only across the final relevant scoped recheck and no-replace tracked placement/readback. Existing-target authentication and verify acquire no primary-mutation lock because they perform no tracked write. Release flock ownership after that critical section but never unlink, replace or recreate the persistent .usf/locks/primary-mutation.lock coordination inode; only the separate per-adoption lock is removable. Perform no validation, history walk, primary Git ref/index change, commit, push, GitHub, provider, CAS, database or network operation while that lock is held." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-historical-currentness-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-historical-currentness-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive adoption state dynamically from exact tracked receipt authentication without a graph edit. The valid receipt permanently records immutable historical carrier identity, scoped classification, durable reachability and point-in-time current observation. Consumers separately rederive live scoped currentness. Ordinary file, graph or HEAD movement cannot require receipt regeneration or reproof; changing a versioned authority resource is an integrity defect and requires a new version rather than rewriting the historical receipt." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:requirement:bootstrap-carrier-noncompletion> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
