<urn:usf:schema:bootstrap-carrier-validation-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonPackageForbiddenField> "packageLinkTopologyDigest" <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:schema:bootstrap-carrier-validation-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:authorityRule> "carrier-tree identity is commit:tree and contentDigest is SHA-256 of a canonical UTF-8 JSON array over the complete recursively parsed raw tree: normalized repository path, raw blob SHA-256 or subtree identity, and raw Git mode. carrier-file identity is one exact validation test or declared receipt/schema input within that tree; contentDigest is SHA-256 of raw blob bytes and fileMode is raw tree mode. package identity is the exact unique pnpm lock package locator, while version and lockIntegrity are its exact authenticated lock values; contentDigest is the installed package-instance file-tree digest and packageLinkTopologyDigest binds that locator's safe lock-derived resolution links. A package file-tree digest hashes the canonical path-ordered array of every regular file's normalized package-relative path, raw SHA-256 and executable or nonexecutable mode. Symlinks are accepted only in the separate lock-derived link-topology array with normalized relative link path and relative target confined beneath the read-only package mount root; absolute, escaping, cyclic, dangling, duplicate or extra links refuse. host-tool identity is the executable name without a host path, version is exact and contentDigest is SHA-256 of executable bytes. authority-resource and confinement-policy identities are exact IRIs and contentDigest is the query-derived resource digest. Unknown kinds, absolute host paths, duplicates, mutable members and caller-authored members refuse." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:rule:bootstrap-carrier-validation-dependencies:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ValidationDependencyDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:rule:bootstrap-carrier-validation-dependencies:1> <urn:usf:predicate:version> "1" <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:rule:bootstrap-carrier-validation-dependencies:1> <urn:usf:predicate:derivationRule> "Derive one finite dependencyMembers set for each validation. Add exactly one carrier-tree member from the authenticated carrier commit/tree. Add carrier-file projections for every carrierBasisTestPath or explicit test path on the selected validation and each graph-declared admission or validation receipt/schema input actually opened; all must resolve within and match the carrier tree. Bind current file-based semantic authority separately through authorityManifestDigest and the finite scoped authority-resource closure, because a later authority manifest cannot be a historical carrier-file member. The complete carrier-tree member binds repository ESM implementation imports, so do not parse TypeScript imports or create another import-discovery implementation. Add host-tool members for the exact git, node and bwrap executables used. Add authority-resource members for the validation, its execution mode and the transition algorithm/timeout policy, plus confinement-policy members for its environment and bootstrap-carrier-no-network. From the exact carrier package.json importer and raw pnpm-lock.yaml digest, add every unique pnpm lock package locator in the lock-closed dependencies, optionalDependencies and test devDependencies closure, each once with its exact version/integrity, installed package-instance file-tree digest and safe link-topology digest. Sort the complete members by kind then identity using unsigned UTF-8 byte order and reject every missing, extra, duplicate or caller-supplied member." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:rule:bootstrap-carrier-validation-dependencies:1> <urn:usf:predicate:packageMountRule> "The repository-local package cache identity is the exact raw carrier pnpm-lock.yaml SHA-256 plus the canonical complete package-closure digest. Before every validation spawn, authenticate every package file tree and safe link topology against its member, construct or reuse only the exact closure as a read-only mount, and immediately recheck the mounted bytes, modes and links. The cache is reconstructable ignored state, never authority. A cache miss, mismatch or unsupported link refuses; verification never fetches, installs, repairs or runs package lifecycle scripts." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
