<urn:usf:digest-membership:bootstrap-carrier-scoped-authority:1> <urn:usf:predicate:digestRule> "Compute one finite subject set. Start with the five fixedClosureRoot values and the exact selected eligibleCarrierAdoption. Expand only: from the algorithm through registeredCommand, resultSchema, receiptBoundary, receiptSchema, receiptDigestMembership, derivedSetDigestMembership, pathEffectSchema, validationResultSchema, validationDependencyDerivationRule, publicationPermission, adoptionStateRule, validationConfinementEnvironment and every requires object; from the selected adoption through transitionAlgorithm, adoptionStateRule, authorityProfile, currentnessAuthority, lineage, pathEffectScope, admissionReceipt and every validation; from the command through topic and outputSchema; from the permission through forAlgorithm and registeredCommand; from the receipt boundary through bootstrapCarrierReceiptSchema; from receipt/result/validation schemas through only digestMembership, derivedSetDigestMembership, pathEffectSchema, adoptedSubjectSchema, validationResultSchema, dependencyMemberSchema and dependencyDerivationRule; from derived digest-membership subjects through canonicalization, memberDigest and aggregateRule; and from each selected validation through environment, executionMode and hostToolDependency. Every other discovered subject is a leaf. Use a visited set for the known reciprocal metadata edges; any missing subject, extra root/member, non-whitelisted expansion or cycle that escapes this allowed finite subject set refuses. The scoped-authority rule itself is a fixed member: include its ordinary query resourceDigest over its authored RDF statements, which is not the generated scopedAuthorityDependencyDigest and therefore creates no recursive digest paradox. Query every subject through the explicit manifest, build objects containing exactly iri and resourceDigest, sort by IRI using unsigned UTF-8 byte order and hash the canonical JSON array. authorityManifestDigest separately binds SHA-256 of the exact raw manifest bytes; observedAuthorityGraphDigest remains a full-graph audit observation rather than a substitute member." <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
<urn:usf:digest-membership:bootstrap-carrier-path-effect-sets:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CanonicalDigestMembership> <urn:usf:graph:integration> .
